Exp:String Operations

Aim:
To write a Java program to perform string operations such as finding the length, converting to uppercase and lowercase, and concatenating two strings.

Algorithm:
1. Start the program.
2. Import the Scanner package.
3. Read two strings from the user.
4. Find the length of the first string.
5. Convert the first string to uppercase and lowercase.
6. Join the two strings using concatenation.
7. Display the results.
8. Stop the program.

Program:

import java.util.Scanner;

public class StringOperation {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        String s1, s2;

        System.out.print("Enter first string: ");
        s1 = sc.nextLine();

        System.out.print("Enter second string: ");
        s2 = sc.nextLine();

        System.out.println("Length = " + s1.length());
        System.out.println("Uppercase = " + s1.toUpperCase());
        System.out.println("Lowercase = " + s1.toLowerCase());
        System.out.println("Concatenation = " + s1.concat(s2));

        sc.close();
    }
}

